# Copy the frontend block to frontend/.env.local.
# Copy the backend block to backend/.env if you run that API.
# Set wallet-service variables in the shell. Do not commit .env or .env.local.
# Do not put seeds, passwords, session tokens, viewing keys, or faucet captcha tokens here.

# Backend API
PORT=4000
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Frontend (frontend/.env.local)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENGINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4010
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_BACKEND=simulated
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_WALLET_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788

# Wallet service (engine/services/wallet-service)
# WALLET_NETWORK=testnet
# WALLET_API_BIND=127.0.0.1:8787
# WALLET_DATA_DIR=./wallet-data
# LIGHTWALLETD_ENDPOINT=https://testnet.zec.rocks:443
# FAUCET_ENDPOINT=https://fauzec.com
# Mainnet wallet service: run a SECOND instance with its own data dir. It spends real ZEC.
# The header network toggle sends requests to port 8788 when mainnet is selected.
# WALLET_NETWORK=mainnet WALLET_API_BIND=127.0.0.1:8788 \
#   WALLET_DATA_DIR=./wallet-data-mainnet LIGHTWALLETD_ENDPOINT=https://zec.rocks:443 \
#   cargo run --release
# The service checks that lightwalletd reports mainnet and refuses a data dir marked testnet.
# Mainnet has no faucet. Spendable funds need 3 confirmations (own change) or 10 (incoming).
# WALLET_BIRTHDAY_HEIGHT is accepted by the parser and ignored at startup.
# It does not restore a wallet.

# Payment engine (engine/, package payment-api)
# PORT=4010
# ENGINE_DB=engine.sqlite
